    {
      "name": "Take Captives",
      "type": "feature",
      "system": {
        "featureForm": "reaction",
        "description": "<p>When a number of pirates equal to the number of PCs in the scene are defeated, roll a <strong>d6</strong>. On a result of 5 or 6, the pirates change tactics, capturing locals and retreating to the ship so they can ransom the captives later. Activate a Consequence Countdown (4). It ticks down when a PC makes an action roll. When it triggers, the pirates sail away with their victims.</p><section id=\"secret-Fiohy1JPx1I5NxnI\" class=\"secret\"><p>Who do the pirates deem the best captives, and why? What do they want in exchange for the captives' return?</p></section>",
